    "content_plain": "\ud83d\udc36 Our mission\nEvery pet should get the care they need, regardless of cost. Vet med prices are up 40% since 2020, and pet owners are stuck having to pick between their bank account and furry friend. At \nSnout\n, we aim to solve this by enabling clinics to offer wellness plans \nthat actually work\n.\n\ud83d\ude80 The opportunity\nSnout is one of the fastest growing wellness plan providers in the veterinary space, trusted by clinics across the U.S. We\u2019re a small but mighty startup team and we\u2019re on the lookout for a \nNurture Clinic Success Manager\n based in our Troy, Michigan office to be the long-term partner that keeps our clinics growing their wellness plan enrollments year after year. \n\ud83d\udcbb The role\nAs a Nurture Clinic Success Manager (CSM), you\u2019ll be the long-term partner and advisor to clinics once their wellness plans are up and running. You\u2019ll build lasting relationships with clinic teams and leadership, run regular business reviews, and bring the ideas and programs that keep enrollments growing. You\u2019ll report to our Head of Clinic Success and work side by side with our Onboarding Specialists and Launch Clinic Success Managers.\nThe Nurture team manages most of our partner clinics. Clinics start with the Launch team, and after their first three months they move to Nurture, where you'll own a book of business. You'll keep those clinics engaged, catch early signs that one is slowing down, and help them grow. That keeps clinics with Snout and pets on their plans, so more pets get affordable preventive care year after year.\nIf you love building relationships that last, can turn a spreadsheet into a clear plan, and get energy from bringing a struggling account back to life, we\u2019d love to hear from you. Come help the pack keep tails wagging for the long haul!\nSnout is committed to building a diverse and inclusive team. We know that great candidates may not check every box \u2014 and that\u2019s okay. If you're excited about this role and our mission, we encourage you to apply if you meet at least 75% of \u201cwhat we\u2019re looking for\u201d including the first bullet point. If you need any accommodations during the application or interview process, please let us know \u2014 we\u2019re happy to support you.\n\ud83d\udee0 What you\u2019ll do\nBuild strong, lasting relationships with clinic teams and leadership\nBe the clinic\u2019s main point of contact after launch\nReach out proactively instead of waiting for clinics to come to you\nRun regular business reviews to track plan performance and clinic health\nMonitor performance, spot clinics that are slipping, and build action plans to improve them\nLead turnaround efforts for clinics that have stalled or haven\u2019t sold plans\nDrive enrollments through ongoing engagement and incentive programs\nPartner with Onboarding Specialists and Launch CSMs when pricing or plan changes are needed\n\ud83d\udca1What we're looking for\n3+ years experience in account management, customer success, or as a Practice Manager or General Manager of a veterinary clinic, human medical clinic, or similar service business\nExcellent relationship-building and account management skills\nComfort leading structured business reviews with clinic leadership\nThe ability to turn performance data into a clear action plan\nStrong problem solving and follow-through\nMotivation to help clinics sustain and grow their results over the long term\n\ud83c\udf1f What will make you stand out\nExperience working in or with veterinary clinics\nYou\u2019ve run staff incentive programs or sales contests and can share the results\nExperience with wellness plans, memberships, or other subscription offerings\nTolerance for working in a fast-paced technology environment with high ambiguity\nAn interest in technology or startups\n\ud83d\udc96 Why you should join Snout\nA chance to be a part of a mission driven company in the pet industry without having to be in clinic\nFast growing, venture capital backed technology company focused on improving access to veterinary care\nAbility to have a meaningful impact from Day 1, where your voice and opinion matters\nUnlimited potential to grow in your career, learn and expand your skillsets\nThis role is in person Monday to Friday in our Troy, MI office but we offer flexibility for your life needs\n\u274c Why this role might not be a fit for you\nYou cannot work in person or cannot make the daily commute to our Troy, MI office\nA fast-paced, technology and startup environment isn\u2019t appealing to you\nYou don\u2019t enjoy working directly with clients, hopping on calls, presenting and teaching others\nWorking alone or on small teams doesn\u2019t sound fun to you\nYou dislike wearing multiple hats or having a heavy workload\nYou can\u2019t handle ambiguity and lack of structure\nOwning a portfolio\u2019s quarter-over-quarter growth and retention sounds more stressful than exciting\n\ud83d\udcb8 Compensation\n$55 000 - $65 000 base salary + bonus plan / $80 000 OTE\n\u2695\ufe0f\nBenefits\nDay 1 medical/dental/vision benefits\nFlexible time off + 11 Snout calendar holidays\nPaid parental leave",
